      "kind": "grammar",
      "title": "Feelings are verbs",
      "text": "In Thai, a word like เหนื่อย (tired), หนาว (cold) or หิว (hungry) needs no \"am/is\": ผมเหนื่อย is just \"I tired\". Put ก็ after the person to say \"also\": ผมก็เหนื่อย (I am tired too).",
